      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $E=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find ${E}^{2}.$\n\n| ${E}^{2}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} | $-3$ | {{field-5}} |  |  |",
